{"lessons":[{"lesson":"When a wake fails because the account hit its usage limit, read the reset time from the wake's log, schedule the next wake just after that time, and clear the alert without spending an LLM wake on it; do not keep firing job, problem and alert wakes into a quota that is known to be empty.","for":"tooling","evidence":"nothing to fix: the first wake after the reset time works; delete the ALERT file"},{"lesson":"Start a chained job once its parent's expected output files are complete, not only when the parent exits with code 0. In this campaign, two kinds of finished job ended FAILED and cancelled the jobs waiting on them: a requeued attempt that hit the launcher's 'refusing to overwrite' guard, and build scripts whose own health rule misfired while their output sets were complete.","for":"tooling","evidence":"never ran (0 of 2 recall passes): its afterok parent 192002 ended FAILED exit 3"},{"lesson":"In the default law and in the budget counter, count a cell only once its job actually starts running, so that a job cancelled before it starts because its parent failed does not use up the cap. Here five such never-run jobs used the cells needed to repeat the single overfit training, so that repeat had to go to the owner.","for":"template","evidence":"A repeat needs 2 cells (training + recall); 1 is left → offered to the owner as option C."},{"lesson":"Read the final 'RESULT key=value' line of a finished job's log into the campaign grid automatically, so the wake does not have to re-send every result by hand with expmon probe.","for":"tooling","evidence":"expmon reads no RESULT line from a log (gripe +1 of 287192bc)"},{"lesson":"In the campaign report, count the hours spent waiting for the owner's answer to an open question separately from idle hours, and show how long that question has been open. This report called 83% of the window idle 'with work outstanding', but all four checks were done and the campaign was only waiting on the owner.","for":"tooling","evidence":"The campaign idled 140.8 h of its 169.0 h window (83%)"}]}
